    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="0841" n="745" xml:id="pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/8729: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-19T18:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1921—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 19—2:10
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>211. Abbott telegraphs from Chita under date of June 17th that the town is quiet
                    and that Ungern’s<anchor n="50" xml:id="d703-f1"/> forces were confronted [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">defeated</hi>] by RedArmy near Verkhneudinsk June
                    6th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d703-f1" n="50" xml:id="d703-f1-content">
                <p>Baron Ungern Sternberg, formerly a captain in the Russian Imperial Army, was
                    advancing from Urga, in Mongolia, which he had captured in February 1921.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
